= [+ pnf_leader +] Appointed Prime Minister!

Popular sentiment within the <span style="color:#0047AB;">bou</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">rge</span><span style="color:#1E99C5;">ois</span> parties against us has led [+ pnf_leader +] and the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">[+ pnf_full_name +]</span> to form an 'Anti-Socialist' coalition and convince the centre-right majority to support him. The King has officially appointed [+ pnf_leader +] as Prime Minister, as many fear he will quickly consolidate power and bring the full force of the government towards us.

He has promised a campaign of staunch anti-socialism, as reports have come out of violence across <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span> already. Contacts between the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">Fasci Italiani di Combattimento</span> and the army has strengthened, as seemingly more military arms appear more frequent in paramilitary hands.

What are we to do now?

- @fight: Mobilise the <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Guards</span> and authorise workers to begin taking up arms against [+ pnf_leader +]'s rule!
- @keep_on: Await our opportunity to strike.


@fight

Do we realize that this means civil war, against the full force of the state?

- @civil_war: Yes.
- @keep_on: We are not ready for war. Instead, we will continue to struggle and await our opportunity.

@keep_on
subtitle: This will not end the game.
on-arrival: next_election_year = 1924; next_election_month = 4; pnf_in_power = 1

We will continue onwards, biding our time. We are facing an extremely uphill battle, and will have to act fast.